<title>UK: Laporte HQ relocation causes 50 job losses.</title>
<headline>Laporte HQ relocation causes 50 job losses.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Laporte Plc said on Tuesday that it was moving its principal corporate office to London, resulting in an overall loss of some 50 jobs.  </p>
<p>The speciality chemicals firm said the relocation would involve the consolidation and closure of its offices in Luton and Bedford Square, central London. It is planned to be completed by the third quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>The 50 job losses at the corporate centre reduce personnel numbers from the current level of 110.</p>
<p>It started a restructuring programme in December 1995, that led to an 83.3 million stg exceptional charge in full year results for 1995.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
